Backport of e5c70e72: the rotate_simple_loops asm peephole converts
header-tested loops (cmp + b.cc at top, unconditional b hdr at latch)
into bottom-tested form - the latch gets a duplicated compare + b.cc
back to the body, the original header stays as the zero-trip guard.
One unconditional branch saved per iteration.

AUDIT NOTES (validated before adoption):
- .LBB labels are globally unique across functions in one emission
  unit (verified on a two-function file), so the text-level
  backedge_count scan cannot cross-match between functions.
- Soundness rests on: single backedge, no calls/rets/indirect branches
  in the loop, header setup limited to <=3 pure flag-preserving
  instructions ending in the Compare the b.cc consumes, and backedge
  phi copies being emitted before the latch branch (register state at
  the latch equals next iteration's header state).
- Lev's task-file edits dropped (his repo's notes, not code).

PROOF: sieve backedge structure changes (19 -> 21 branch lines: the
duplicated cmp+b.cc pair replaces one b), qemu output 664579 identical,
qemu wall time 0.68s -> 0.62s (-9%). 663 lib tests, ARM differential
holds 94/30, x86 164/164 untouched (arm-only file).
CCC_NO_LOOP_ROTATE=1 escape hatch preserved.
