Subject: [PATCH 3/3] adopt affine marching-pointer alias analysis in
 loop_memory_promote

Backport of levkropp 57ab50aa (his newest commit): loop_memory_promote
runs to a fixpoint (multi-promote) and gains a linear-form engine that
resolves pointers to root + sum(coeff*iv) + konst + march*t. A
loop-invariant candidate is provably disjoint from a marching store
when roots and symbolic parts match and the store range marches away
from the candidate (nbody j-loop shape: bodies[i].vx vs bodies[j].vx,
j=i+1.., stride 56).

AUDIT (this pass family caused the sqlite 'SELECT 1.5' infinite hang;
maximum suspicion applied):
- The disjointness proof requires: identical roots (globals hashed by
  name, allocas/params by id), identical symbolic terms, candidate
  loop-invariant AND march-free, and the march direction strictly away
  from the candidate range including size. Overflow-checked arithmetic
  throughout; fuel-limited resolution; unknown defs become opaque roots
  which then fail the root-equality test - fail closed.
- Adversarial regression test loop_promote_affine_alias.c: nbody shape
  (numeric identity 6.075000 vs gcc on x86 AND aarch64/qemu),
  march-down-hits-candidate, strided-store gaps, row/column diagonal
  crossing. All pass on x86 + ARM.
